                    briefingEs: 'Ha llegado a la mesa de negociación del Proyecto Salar Larache, un proyecto de extracción de litio con un VPN de $1,800M a 25 años. Cuatro grupos de interés han presentado sus posiciones iniciales:<br><br><strong>CORMIN</strong> (Gobierno): Exige una regalía del 32%, 500 empleos locales, un centro de capacitación y una participación accionaria del 15%.<br><strong>Comunidad Atacameña</strong> (Comunidad Indígena): Exige cero extracción de agua subterránea, veto total, 35% de empleo y protección de sitios sagrados.<br><strong>Meridian Capital</strong> (Inversionistas): Requiere 18% TIR, seguro de riesgo político completo y regalía tope de 22%.<br><strong>Alianza por los Salares</strong> (ONGs Ambientales): Exige moratoria de cinco años, estudio de línea base independiente y zonas de exclusión de 3km.<br><br>A nivel posicional, no hay acuerdo posible. Su tarea: elaborar su primera propuesta integral.',
                    eventEn: null,
                    eventEs: null
                },
                {
                    briefingEn: 'Your initial conversations have revealed hints about underlying interests beneath the stated positions:<br><br><strong>CORMIN</strong> mentioned: "What matters most is that the people of this region see real benefit from this project." This suggests political visibility and fiscal certainty may matter more than the raw royalty percentage.<br><strong>Comunidad Atacameña</strong> expressed: "We have seen promises before. Show us proof that the water will be protected." Their core concern appears to be verifiable water security, not absolute prohibition.<br><strong>Meridian Capital</strong> noted: "Our ESG fund mandate is commercially existential. A certified sustainable deal may be worth more than a higher nominal return." Risk reduction could lower their IRR requirement.<br><strong>Alianza por los Salares</strong> stated: "We need independent monitoring with real data access. That is what has been missing in every previous project." Transparency may substitute for a moratorium.<br><br>Revise your package based on these interest signals.',
                    briefingEs: 'Sus conversaciones iniciales revelaron indicios sobre los intereses subyacentes detrás de las posiciones declaradas:<br><br><strong>CORMIN</strong> mencionó: "Lo que más importa es que la gente de esta región vea beneficios reales de este proyecto." Esto sugiere que la visibilidad política y la certeza fiscal pueden importar más que el porcentaje bruto de regalía.<br><strong>Comunidad Atacameña</strong> expresó: "Ya hemos visto promesas antes. Demuéstrenos que el agua estará protegida." Su preocupación central parece ser la seguridad hídrica verificable, no la prohibición absoluta.<br><strong>Meridian Capital</strong> señaló: "Nuestro mandato de fondo ESG es comercialmente existencial. Un acuerdo certificado como sostenible puede valer más que un retorno nominal mayor." La reducción de riesgo podría reducir su requisito de TIR.<br><strong>Alianza por los Salares</strong> declaró: "Necesitamos monitoreo independiente con acceso real a datos. Eso es lo que ha faltado en cada proyecto anterior." La transparencia podría sustituir a la moratoria.<br><br>Revise su paquete basándose en estas señales de interés.',
                    eventEn: '⚠️ <strong>Crisis Event:</strong> A journalist reports that representatives of GigaLitio Corp — a Chinese state-owned enterprise — were seen meeting with CORMIN officials in Santiago. GigaLitio has been lobbying for license reversion. The pressure to close a deal has intensified significantly.',
                    eventEs: '⚠️ <strong>Evento de Crisis:</strong> Un periodista reporta que representantes de GigaLitio Corp — una empresa estatal china — fueron vistos reuniéndose con funcionarios de CORMIN en Santiago. GigaLitio ha estado presionando por la reversión de la licencia. La presión para cerrar un acuerdo se ha intensificado significativamente.'
                },
                {
                    briefingEn: 'Your intelligence team has uncovered critical information that reshapes the negotiation landscape:<br><br>📊 <strong>CORMIN:</strong> Minimum acceptable royalty is actually 22% (not 32%). They will accept this rate if job creation targets and institutional oversight are strong. The 15% equity demand was a late addition — not a real priority.<br>📊 <strong>Comunidad:</strong> True priority ranking is: (1) Water monitoring, (2) Employment and skills development, (3) Territorial recognition. The zero-extraction demand is positional — they will accept monitored extraction with real-time community data access.<br>📊 <strong>Meridian:</strong> Minimum IRR drops to 15.5% if the deal includes certified FPIC and Article 9-compliant environmental framework. ESG compliance is worth more than 2.5 percentage points of return.<br>📊 <strong>Alianza:</strong> Three of seven member NGOs privately support a well-designed project. The coalition requires four NGOs to maintain a blocking stance. A strong monitoring framework could split the coalition favorably.<br><br>This is your chance to redesign your offer around interests, not positions. The ZOPA is substantial — if you can find it.',
                    briefingEs: 'Su equipo de inteligencia ha descubierto información crítica que redefine el panorama de la negociación:<br><br>📊 <strong>CORMIN:</strong> La regalía mínima aceptable es realmente 22% (no 32%). Aceptarán esta tasa si las metas de creación de empleo y la supervisión institucional son sólidas. La demanda de 15% de participación fue una adición tardía — no es una prioridad real.<br>📊 <strong>Comunidad:</strong> La priorización real es: (1) Monitoreo de agua, (2) Empleo y desarrollo de habilidades, (3) Reconocimiento territorial. La demanda de cero extracción es posicional — aceptarán extracción monitoreada con acceso comunitario a datos en tiempo real.<br>📊 <strong>Meridian:</strong> La TIR mínima baja a 15.5% si el acuerdo incluye CLPI certificado y marco ambiental conforme al Artículo 9. El cumplimiento ESG vale más que 2.5 puntos porcentuales de retorno.<br>📊 <strong>Alianza:</strong> Tres de siete ONGs miembros apoyan privadamente un proyecto bien diseñado. La coalición requiere cuatro ONGs para mantener una postura de bloqueo. Un marco de monitoreo sólido podría dividir favorablemente la coalición.<br><br>Esta es su oportunidad de rediseñar su oferta en torno a intereses, no posiciones. La ZOPA es sustancial — si puede encontrarla.',
                    eventEn: '📋 <strong>Coalition Intelligence:</strong> The Alianza and the Comunidad have been in direct contact. The Alianza is supporting the water monitoring demand in exchange for the Comunidad backing public data disclosure requirements. Consider a package that addresses both parties simultaneously.',
                    eventEs: '📋 <strong>Inteligencia de Coalición:</strong> La Alianza y la Comunidad han estado en contacto directo. La Alianza apoya la demanda de monitoreo de agua a cambio de que la Comunidad respalde los requisitos de divulgación pública de datos. Considere un paquete que aborde a ambas partes simultáneamente.'
                },
                {
                    briefingEn: '🏛️ <strong>THE STAKEHOLDER SUMMIT</strong><br><br>All four stakeholder groups are now at the table simultaneously. This is your final opportunity to present a comprehensive package before the exploration license expires.<br><br>Each stakeholder will evaluate your final proposal against their true interests and walk-away positions. They will each decide independently to <strong>Sign</strong> or <strong>Withhold</strong>.<br><br>A unanimous signature secures the Project Development Agreement. If any party withholds, the deal collapses and GigaLitio moves in.<br><br>Remember: the optimal deal creates value for all parties simultaneously. Royalty-for-Oversight. Monitoring-for-Moratorium. Community enterprise instead of employment quotas. ESG certification for IRR reduction. Graduated royalty for volume certainty.<br><br>Present your best and final offer.',
                    briefingEs: '🏛️ <strong>LA CUMBRE DE PARTES INTERESADAS</strong><br><br>Los cuatro grupos de interés están ahora en la mesa simultáneamente. Esta es su última oportunidad de presentar un paquete integral antes de que expire la licencia de exploración.<br><br>Cada parte evaluará su propuesta final contra sus verdaderos intereses y posiciones de retiro. Cada uno decidirá de forma independiente si <strong>Firma</strong> o <strong>Retiene</strong>.<br><br>Una firma unánime asegura el Acuerdo de Desarrollo del Proyecto. Si cualquier parte retiene, el acuerdo colapsa y GigaLitio avanza.<br><br>Recuerde: el acuerdo óptimo crea valor para todas las partes simultáneamente. Regalía-por-Supervisión. Monitoreo-por-Moratoria. Fondo empresarial comunitario en lugar de cuotas de empleo. Certificación ESG por reducción de TIR. Regalía progresiva por certeza de volumen.<br><br>Presente su oferta mejor y final.',
                    eventEn: null,
                    eventEs: null
                }
            ];
        }

        initialize(state) {
            // Reseed when the domainState is missing OR when there is no submitted
            // history. The framework calls initialize() again after undoing the first
            // round; v1.0.0's `Object.keys(...).length === 0` guard never fired then,
            // so the post-round-1 trust values and chart history survived the undo and
            // the replayed round pushed a duplicate entry.
            var noHistory = !state.history || state.history.length === 0;
            if (!state.domainState || Object.keys(state.domainState).length === 0 || noHistory) {
                state.domainState = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(this.SEED));
            }
            if (!state.decisions || Object.keys(state.decisions).length === 0) {
                state.decisions = {
                    royaltyRate: 24,
                    waterMonitoring: 5,
                    communityFund: 15,
                    envSafeguards: 3,
                    offeredIRR: 16
                };
            }
            this._syncUI(state);
        }

        // ---------- pure model ----------
        _satisfactions(d) {
            var rNorm = (d.royaltyRate - 18) / 14;
            var wNorm = d.waterMonitoring / 15;
            var cNorm = d.communityFund / 45;
            var eNorm = (d.envSafeguards - 1) / 4;
            var iNorm = (d.offeredIRR - 14) / 4;
            var sw = this.STAKEHOLDER_WEIGHTS;
            function clamp(v) { return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(v))); }
            return {
                cormin: clamp((rNorm * sw.cormin.royalty + wNorm * sw.cormin.water + cNorm * sw.cormin.community
                              + eNorm * sw.cormin.env + (1 - iNorm) * sw.cormin.irrLow) * 100),
                comunidad: clamp((rNorm * sw.comunidad.royalty + wNorm * sw.comunidad.water + cNorm * sw.comunidad.community
                              + eNorm * sw.comunidad.env) * 100),
                meridian: clamp(((1 - rNorm) * sw.meridian.royaltyLow + wNorm * sw.meridian.water + cNorm * sw.meridian.community
                              + eNorm * sw.meridian.env + iNorm * sw.meridian.irrHigh) * 100),
                alianza: clamp((rNorm * sw.alianza.royalty + wNorm * sw.alianza.water + cNorm * sw.alianza.community
                              + eNorm * sw.alianza.env) * 100)
            };
        }

        _npv(d) {
            return Math.max(0, Math.round(
                1800
                - (d.royaltyRate - 18) * 30
                - d.waterMonitoring * 1
                - d.communityFund * 0.6
                - (d.envSafeguards - 1) * 8
                - (d.offeredIRR - 14) * 45
            ));
        }

        // Single scoring function: used every round (so the grading layer always has a
        // score) and by getPerformanceSummary(), so the two can never diverge.
        _score(snapshot) {
            var s = snapshot;
            var signed = (s.corminSigned ? 1 : 0) + (s.comunidadSigned ? 1 : 0)
                       + (s.meridianSigned ? 1 : 0) + (s.alianzaSigned ? 1 : 0);
            var avgSat = (s.corminSat + s.comunidadSat + s.meridianSat + s.alianzaSat) / 4;
            var trustAvg = (s.corminTrust + s.comunidadTrust + s.meridianTrust + s.alianzaTrust) / 4;

            var valueScore   = Math.min(100, (s.npv / 1800) * 100) * 0.30;
            var zopaScore    = avgSat * 0.25;
            var processScore = Math.min(100, (avgSat * 0.5 + (signed / 4) * 50)) * 0.20;
            var trustScore   = trustAvg * 0.15;
            var summitScore  = (signed / 4) * 100 * 0.10;
            var dealBonus    = (signed === 4) ? 1.15 : 1.0;

            // v1.0.0 could return up to 115 on a 0-100 grade scale; clamped.
            var total = Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(100,
                (valueScore + zopaScore + processScore + trustScore + summitScore) * dealBonus)));

            return { total: total, signed: signed, avgSat: avgSat, trustAvg: trustAvg };
        }

        _fail(key, fallback) {
            var msg = this._t(key, fallback);
            var box = document.getElementById('validationError');
            if (box) {
                box.textContent = msg;
                box.style.display = 'block';
            }
            try {
                window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(msg, 'warning');
            } catch (e) { /* notification is best-effort */ }
            return false;
        }

        _clearError() {
            var box = document.getElementById('validationError');
            if (box) { box.textContent = ''; box.style.display = 'none'; }
        }

        validateDecisions(decisions) {
            var num = function(id, parser) {
                var el = document.getElementById(id);
                if (!el) return undefined;
                var v = parser(el.value);
                return isFinite(v) ? v : NaN;   // v1.0.0 let NaN/'' through some branches
            };

            var royalty  = num('royaltyInput', parseFloat);
            var water    = num('waterInput', parseFloat);
            var community= num('communityInput', parseFloat);
            var env      = num('envInput', parseInt);
            var irr      = num('irrInput', parseFloat);

            if (royalty   !== undefined) decisions.royaltyRate     = royalty;
            if (water     !== undefined) decisions.waterMonitoring = water;
            if (community !== undefined) decisions.communityFund   = community;
            if (env       !== undefined) decisions.envSafeguards   = env;
            if (irr       !== undefined) decisions.offeredIRR      = irr;

            var d = decisions;
            var ok = function(v, lo, hi) { return typeof v === 'number' && isFinite(v) && v >= lo && v <= hi; };

            if (!ok(d.royaltyRate, 18, 32))      return this._fail('royalty_warning',   'Royalty rate must be between 18% and 32%');
            if (!ok(d.waterMonitoring, 0, 15))   return this._fail('water_warning',     'Water monitoring must be between $0M and $15M');
            if (!ok(d.communityFund, 0, 45))     return this._fail('community_warning', 'Community fund must be between $0M and $45M');
            if (!ok(d.envSafeguards, 1, 5))      return this._fail('env_warning',       'Environmental level must be between 1 and 5');
            if (!ok(d.offeredIRR, 14, 18))       return this._fail('irr_warning',       'IRR must be between 14% and 18%');

            this._clearError();
            return true;
        }

        calculateResults(state) {
            var d = state.decisions;
            var ds = state.domainState;

            var sat = this._satisfactions(d);
            var corminSat = sat.cormin, comunidadSat = sat.comunidad,
                meridianSat = sat.meridian, alianzaSat = sat.alianza;

            var roundMultiplier = 1 + (state.currentPeriod - 1) * 0.1;

            ds.corminTrust    = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(ds.corminTrust    + (corminSat    - 50) * 0.35 * roundMultiplier)));
            ds.comunidadTrust = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(ds.comunidadTrust + (comunidadSat - 50) * 0.40 * roundMultiplier)));
            ds.meridianTrust  = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(ds.meridianTrust  + (meridianSat  - 50) * 0.30 * roundMultiplier)));
            ds.alianzaTrust   = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(ds.alianzaTrust   + (alianzaSat   - 50) * 0.38 * roundMultiplier)));

            ds.ecoLitioNPV = this._npv(d);

            var avgSat = (corminSat + comunidadSat + meridianSat + alianzaSat) / 4;
            ds.aggregateSatisfaction = Math.round(avgSat);
            ds.zopaUtilization = Math.round(avgSat);

            ds.corminSigned    = corminSat    >= this.SIGN_THRESHOLDS.cormin    && ds.corminTrust    >= 40;
            ds.comunidadSigned = comunidadSat >= this.SIGN_THRESHOLDS.comunidad && ds.comunidadTrust >= 30;
            ds.meridianSigned  = meridianSat  >= this.SIGN_THRESHOLDS.meridian  && ds.meridianTrust  >= 40;
            ds.alianzaSigned   = alianzaSat   >= this.SIGN_THRESHOLDS.alianza   && ds.alianzaTrust   >= 30;

            var lastRound = state.maxPeriods || 4;   // v1.0.0 hard-coded `=== 4`
            if (state.currentPeriod >= lastRound) {
                ds.dealOutcome = (ds.corminSigned && ds.comunidadSigned && ds.meridianSigned && ds.alianzaSigned)
                    ? 'signed' : 'failed';
            } else {
                ds.dealOutcome = 'negotiating';
            }

            ds.corminTrustHistory.push(ds.corminTrust);
            ds.comunidadTrustHistory.push(ds.comunidadTrust);
            ds.meridianTrustHistory.push(ds.meridianTrust);
            ds.alianzaTrustHistory.push(ds.alianzaTrust);
            ds.npvHistory.push(ds.ecoLitioNPV);
            ds.zopaHistory.push(ds.zopaUtilization);
            ds.corminSatHistory.push(corminSat);
            ds.comunidadSatHistory.push(comunidadSat);
            ds.meridianSatHistory.push(meridianSat);
            ds.alianzaSatHistory.push(alianzaSat);

            var snapshot = {
                corminSat: corminSat, comunidadSat: comunidadSat, meridianSat: meridianSat, alianzaSat: alianzaSat,
                corminTrust: ds.corminTrust, comunidadTrust: ds.comunidadTrust,
                meridianTrust: ds.meridianTrust, alianzaTrust: ds.alianzaTrust,
                npv: ds.ecoLitioNPV,
                corminSigned: ds.corminSigned, comunidadSigned: ds.comunidadSigned,
                meridianSigned: ds.meridianSigned, alianzaSigned: ds.alianzaSigned
            };
            var sc = this._score(snapshot);

            // Grading contract (results_utils.php :: express_resolveDomainScore):
            // domainState.performance.overallScore, else a top-level numeric score.
            // v1.0.0 only computed a score inside getPerformanceSummary(), so the
            // instructor panel showed "—" and the exported grade was empty.
            ds.performance = ds.performance || {};
            ds.performance.overallScore = sc.total;
            ds.score = sc.total;

            // NOTE: calculateResults() must stay pure — usf-engine.js
            // _computeCompetitionPreview() runs it on a clone on every input change.
            // v1.0.0 wrote the trust bars and scheduled a briefing rebuild from here,
            // so previewing overwrote the real UI. DOM updates now happen in _syncUI(),
            // driven by the afterAdvance / period:undone lifecycle.
            return {
                period: state.currentPeriod,
                royaltyRate: d.royaltyRate,
                waterMonitoring: d.waterMonitoring,
                communityFund: d.communityFund,
                envSafeguards: d.envSafeguards,
                offeredIRR: d.offeredIRR,
                corminSat: corminSat,
                comunidadSat: comunidadSat,
                meridianSat: meridianSat,
                alianzaSat: alianzaSat,
                corminTrust: ds.corminTrust,
                comunidadTrust: ds.comunidadTrust,
                meridianTrust: ds.meridianTrust,
                alianzaTrust: ds.alianzaTrust,
                npv: ds.ecoLitioNPV,
                zopaUtilization: ds.zopaUtilization,
                aggregateSatisfaction: ds.aggregateSatisfaction,
                dealOutcome: ds.dealOutcome,
                corminSigned: ds.corminSigned,
                comunidadSigned: ds.comunidadSigned,
                meridianSigned: ds.meridianSigned,
                alianzaSigned: ds.alianzaSigned,
                score: sc.total
            };
        }

        _t(key, fallback) {
            try {
                var s = window.mySimulation;
                if (s && typeof s.t === 'function') {
                    var v = s.t(key);
                    if (v && v !== key) return v;
                }
            } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
            return fallback;
        }

        _lang() {
            try {
                return (window.mySimulation && window.mySimulation.lang) || 'en';
            } catch (e) { return 'en'; }
        }

        // Single UI refresh point: briefing, event alert, trust bars and the
        // per-stakeholder sign/withhold chips. Called from initialize(), from the
        // afterAdvance hook and from period:undone — never from calculateResults().
        _syncUI(state) {
            if (!state) return;
            var ds = state.domainState || {};
            this._updateBriefing(state);
            this._updateTrustBars(ds);
            this._updateSignChips(state);
        }

        _updateTrustBars(ds) {
            var map = {
                corminTrustBar: ds.corminTrust,
                comunidadTrustBar: ds.comunidadTrust,
                meridianTrustBar: ds.meridianTrust,
                alianzaTrustBar: ds.alianzaTrust
            };
            for (var id in map) {
                var el = document.getElementById(id);
                if (el && typeof map[id] === 'number') {
                    el.style.width = map[id] + '%';
                    el.setAttribute('aria-valuenow', String(map[id]));
                }
            }
        }

        // v1.0.0 computed *Signed every round but never showed it until the final
        // outcome — players had no idea who was above their signing threshold.
        _updateSignChips(state) {
            var ds = state.domainState || {};
            var played = (ds.corminSatHistory || []).length > 0;
            var parties = [
                ['cormin', ds.corminSigned], ['comunidad', ds.comunidadSigned],
                ['meridian', ds.meridianSigned], ['alianza', ds.alianzaSigned]
            ];
            for (var i = 0; i < parties.length; i++) {
                var el = document.getElementById(parties[i][0] + 'SignChip');
                if (!el) continue;
                if (!played) {
                    el.textContent = this._t('chip_pending', 'Awaiting first offer');
                    el.className = 'ecolitio-sim-sign-chip ecolitio-chip-pending';
                } else if (parties[i][1]) {
                    el.textContent = this._t('chip_would_sign', '✓ Would sign');
                    el.className = 'ecolitio-sim-sign-chip ecolitio-chip-sign';
                } else {
                    el.textContent = this._t('chip_would_withhold', '✗ Would withhold');
                    el.className = 'ecolitio-sim-sign-chip ecolitio-chip-withhold';
                }
            }
        }

        _updateBriefing(state) {
            var idx = Math.min(Math.max((state.currentPeriod || 1) - 1, 0), this.ROUNDS.length - 1);
            var round = this.ROUNDS[idx];
            var lang = this._lang();

            var briefEl = document.getElementById('briefingText');
            if (briefEl) {
                briefEl.innerHTML = lang === 'es' ? round.briefingEs : round.briefingEn;
            }

            var eventEl = document.getElementById('eventAlert');
            if (eventEl) {
                var eventText = lang === 'es' ? round.eventEs : round.eventEn;
                if (eventText) {
                    eventEl.innerHTML = eventText;
                    eventEl.style.display = 'block';
                } else {
                    eventEl.innerHTML = '';
                    eventEl.style.display = 'none';
                }
            }
        }

        setupUI(uiManager) {
            uiManager.bind('currentDay', 'currentPeriod');
            uiManager.bind('maxPeriods', 'maxPeriods');
            uiManager.bind('corminTrustDisplay', 'domainState.corminTrust');
            uiManager.bind('comunidadTrustDisplay', 'domainState.comunidadTrust');
            uiManager.bind('meridianTrustDisplay', 'domainState.meridianTrust');
            uiManager.bind('alianzaTrustDisplay', 'domainState.alianzaTrust');
            uiManager.bind('npvDisplay', 'domainState.ecoLitioNPV',
                function(v) { return '$' + Math.round(v).toLocaleString() + 'M'; });
            uiManager.bind('zopaDisplay', 'domainState.zopaUtilization',
                function(v) { return v + '%'; });
            uiManager.bind('satisfactionDisplay', 'domainState.aggregateSatisfaction');
            uiManager.bind('scoreDisplay', 'domainState.score',
                function(v) { return (v || 0) + '/100'; });
            var self = this;
            uiManager.bind('outcomeDisplay', 'domainState.dealOutcome',
                function(v) {
                    if (v === 'signed') return '✅ ' + self._t('status_signed', 'Deal Signed');
                    if (v === 'failed') return '❌ ' + self._t('status_failed', 'Deal Failed');
                    return '🔄 ' + self._t('status_negotiating', 'Negotiating');
                });

            // Lifecycle-driven UI refresh. v1.0.0 rebuilt the briefing from a
            // setTimeout inside calculateResults(); the callback read
            // state.currentPeriod + 1 when it *fired* — after the framework had
            // already advanced the period — so submitting round 1 displayed round 3's
            // briefing, and the competition preview rebuilt it mid-decision.
            var sim = window.mySimulation;
            if (sim && sim.periodManager && typeof sim.periodManager.addHook === 'function') {
                sim.periodManager.addHook('afterAdvance', function(st) { self._syncUI(st); });
            }
            if (sim && sim.eventBus && typeof sim.eventBus.on === 'function') {
                sim.eventBus.on('period:undone', function(st) { self._syncUI(st); });
                sim.eventBus.on('language:changed', function() {
                    self._syncUI(sim.state);   // briefing/event text were stuck in the old language
                });
            }
        }

        getChartConfig() {
            var _tc = (window.mySimulation && typeof window.mySimulation.t === 'function') ? window.mySimulation.t.bind(window.mySimulation) : function(k) { return k; };
            return {
                trustChart: {
                    type: 'line',
                    data: {
                        labels: [],
                        datasets: [
                            {
                                label: 'CORMIN',
